00:12:26.366 --> 00:12:29.494
Californians, couldn't
point Arizona on the map.

00:12:29.494 --> 00:12:32.577
The guy said it's sort of in this area.

00:12:32.577 --> 00:12:34.082
How do you not know where Arizona is?

00:12:34.082 --> 00:12:35.321
(audience laughing)

00:12:35.321 --> 00:12:38.535
Do you think that if you
didn't know where Arizona

00:12:38.535 --> 00:12:41.103
was you might have had that
straight A education but

00:12:41.103 --> 00:12:43.104
you got in the lunch room and
they're going to say fired.

00:12:43.104 --> 00:12:45.415
What do you think?

00:12:45.415 --> 00:12:47.353
I mean there's just certain
things, I mean how many

00:12:47.353 --> 00:12:49.360
of you knew last summer there
was a flood in Pakistan?

00:12:49.360 --> 00:12:51.426
What are you going to talk
about when you get out in

00:12:51.426 --> 00:12:53.045
the real world if you
don't have any knowledge

00:12:53.045 --> 00:12:54.647
of current events?

00:12:54.647 --> 00:12:57.372
How do you have any way of
assimilating your education

00:12:57.372 --> 00:12:59.539
in some sort of context if
you don't have a knowledge

00:12:59.539 --> 00:13:01.039
of current events?

00:13:02.615 --> 00:13:05.246
I was always a current events
junkie, I'd go home at 4:00

00:13:05.246 --> 00:13:07.106
and watch news until 7:00.

00:13:07.106 --> 00:13:09.496
Maybe I took it to the
extreme, but I wake up in the

00:13:09.496 --> 00:13:11.450
middle of the night and I
watch the BBC for five minutes

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:13.223
to find out what the hell's
gone on since I went to bed.

00:13:13.223 --> 00:13:15.050
I'm really curious.

00:13:15.050 --> 00:13:16.246
(audience laughing)

00:13:16.246 --> 00:13:18.055
You ever read a good book,
you just can't wait for

00:13:18.055 --> 00:13:19.487
the next chapter?

00:13:19.487 --> 00:13:21.113
Never happened to me,
but I hear you can do it.

00:13:21.113 --> 00:13:23.191
(audience laughing)

00:13:23.191 --> 00:13:25.358
But the news is like that.

00:13:27.188 --> 00:13:29.879
- So you heard from Mr.
Orafalea himself, my students,

00:13:29.879 --> 00:13:31.954
be curious, pay attention.

00:13:31.954 --> 00:13:34.599
- And watch the paper, read
the paper, read the news.

00:13:34.599 --> 00:13:35.599
Be involved.

00:13:37.886 --> 00:13:39.982
You want to hear another
great stupid story?

00:13:39.982 --> 00:13:42.322
(audience laughing)

00:13:42.322 --> 00:13:45.139
They got his McKinsey, you
ever heard of McKinsey?

00:13:45.139 --> 00:13:47.124
(audience laughing)

00:13:47.124 --> 00:13:49.113
Are they here or something?

00:13:49.113 --> 00:13:51.970
So I leave the company, they
spent $2 million to study

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:53.553
our business, okay?

00:13:55.478 --> 00:13:59.423
I was talking to this man
and he owned these markets

00:13:59.423 --> 00:14:02.498
called (bleep) Markets in
Pennsylvania, you ever see them?

00:14:02.498 --> 00:14:07.124
Okay, guy tells me at lunch,
you know I can't explain

00:14:07.124 --> 00:14:10.418
it but we would close our
business from midnight to 6 in

00:14:10.418 --> 00:14:15.244
the morning cuz we'd only
do $40 in business but our

00:14:15.244 --> 00:14:18.244
daytime business would drop in half.

00:14:19.787 --> 00:14:22.379
He said I don't understand why
just closing those six hours

00:14:22.379 --> 00:14:24.754
would have such an effect
on my daytime business.

00:14:24.754 --> 00:14:28.671
What did the guy tell
you, I go to bed, I go to

00:14:29.696 --> 00:14:32.265
sleep I wake up like a bat
out of hell and I said,

00:14:32.265 --> 00:14:34.859
what'd the guy tell you,
if you go 24 hours a day,

00:14:34.859 --> 00:14:37.167
your daytime business
doubles, is that correct?

00:14:37.167 --> 00:14:40.321
And it's true, and it
doubled, my overhead was the

00:14:40.321 --> 00:14:43.970
same everything, it was
all marginal profit.

00:14:43.970 --> 00:14:46.410
Was that a cool discovery?

00:14:46.410 --> 00:14:49.565
Let's go like this, yeah
it was a good discovery.

00:14:49.565 --> 00:14:51.333
(audience laughing)

00:14:51.333 --> 00:14:53.330
So the bozos get this
McKinsey in there and McKinsey

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:55.187
takes a stopwatch and says
by the way you'll save

00:14:55.187 --> 00:14:57.475
a bunch of money closing
at 10 at night and opening

00:14:57.475 --> 00:14:59.330
up at 6 in the morning.

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:01.247
Was the wrong decision?

00:15:02.504 --> 00:15:04.946
You know the art of business
is seeing what isn't there,

00:15:04.946 --> 00:15:07.096
anybody can see what's
there but the art is seeing

00:15:07.096 --> 00:15:09.023
what isn't there.

00:15:09.023 --> 00:15:11.209
Did anybody see that half
the customers I lost cuz I

00:15:11.209 --> 00:15:12.292
wasn't there?

00:15:14.167 --> 00:15:17.966
But that's another thing that
maybe you guys don't see,

00:15:17.966 --> 00:15:19.695
you don't see what isn't there.

00:15:19.695 --> 00:15:21.572
Maybe you should go home
and have some more anxiety.

00:15:21.572 --> 00:15:24.564
There's only one measure
of success in this world.

00:15:24.564 --> 00:15:26.397
You know what that is?

00:15:28.469 --> 00:15:30.355
Do your children want to be
with you when they're adults?

00:15:30.355 --> 00:15:33.455
Don't forget, if you get so
busy your children don't ever

00:15:33.455 --> 00:15:37.759
want to come home and see
you, I don't know if that's

00:15:37.759 --> 00:15:40.828
really being successful, so
it's very tricky marketing

00:15:40.828 --> 00:15:44.054
to your kids cuz you want
to raise them and be strict

00:15:44.054 --> 00:15:47.690
but at the same time you
want them to come home for

00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:48.962
Christmas.

00:15:48.962 --> 00:15:50.729
How do you do that?

00:15:50.729 --> 00:15:53.055
If you become too strict they
don't want to come home ever?

00:15:53.055 --> 00:15:54.523
You're a jerk, if you're
too lenient they become

00:15:54.523 --> 00:15:55.616
drug addicts, I don't know.

00:15:55.616 --> 00:15:56.449
(audience laughing)

